{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nCumulative error counters in infra/scripts/observability.sh persist an acknowledgement offset before CloudWatch accepts the matching datapoint. A transient put-metric-data failure therefore causes the next interval to compute zero from an already-advanced baseline, permanently losing the positive delta. The same copied construct affects seven metric streams across six code shapes, including the G2P block omitted from the original five-site census.\n\n## Proven root cause\n\nEach affected block writes total to its offset file before running aws cloudwatch put-metric-data. Whole-script runtime probes showed offset 2/source 7/failing AWS becomes offset 7, and the next successful run publishes 0 rather than 5 for every stream. Removing only error suppression does not recover the count. Original feature stories explicitly require these observed failures to publish metrics and trip alarms.\n\n## Repair plan\n\n- Reorder each of the six concrete publish shapes so the matching offset advances only after a successful CloudWatch call. Cover replication, voter, merge-change, deploy, both shared autodeploy-marker streams, and G2P.\n- Preserve the script systemd exit-0 contract and existing logging behavior: AWS failure stays best-effort for the overall probe, but the failed metric remains unacknowledged.\n- Keep zero-delta publication behavior unchanged; a successful zero publish may acknowledge the observed total. Preserve reset handling where total below offset retries total.\n- Add a whole-script PATH-shim regression oracle that drives the real script, fails each targeted AWS metric once, proves the offset is byte-identical after failure, then proves a successful retry publishes the accumulated delta and advances the offset. Include zero/reset controls and both shared-helper metrics.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Run `pytest -q tests/scripts/test_observability_offsets_6a65.py tests/scripts/test_observability_exit.py`.\n- Run `make lint` and `make typecheck`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] All seven cumulative counter streams advance their offset only after the matching successful AWS publication, checked by the whole-script test.\n- [ ] A failed publication leaves the targeted offset byte-identical, checked for every stream by the whole-script test.\n- [ ] A subsequent successful run publishes the accumulated delta and then advances the offset, checked for every stream.\n- [ ] Reset handling retries the reset total after failure, and zero-delta behavior remains compatible.\n- [ ] observability.sh still exits zero when an individual AWS publication fails and on a healthy run.\n- [ ] The held-out oracle is observed RED before the fix, GREEN after the fix, and RED again under the original pre-acknowledgement mutation.\n- [ ] Repository lint and typecheck gates pass."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786300530649345001,"uuid":"6134aa33-a85e-48a4-a093-b79744cf204f"}